{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them","id":1246864,"title":"Getimians: What Am I Supposed To Do With Them?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-16T21:22:40-07:00","id":1246864,"title":"Getimians: What Am I Supposed To Do With Them?","content":"So, the 3e corebook gives a pretty good idea of where Liminals and Exigents fit into Creation and I can understand how one would incorporate characters and factions focused around them into a story. But the last new Exalted, the Getimians, leave me at a loss. It's an entire splat that we have no information on. What do they do? What <i>can </i>they do, other than hate the Sidereals and like that the Lunars also hate the Sidereals? Our current idea of their powers, themes and agenda is so vague, I don't even know where to start making things up.<br /> <br /> Has anyone ever used them? What did you do with them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T21:33:44-07:00","id":1246867,"title":"","content":"We know a few things about Getmetians. We know they have pattern spiders in their spine that weave their own fates. We know that they have a war with Heaven--not merely the Sidereals--and I beleive they are related to fates that could have been. I've heard also that you could think of Getmetians as people who are intentionally causing glitches in a videogame for their advantage....<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T21:53:25-07:00","id":1246872,"title":"","content":"Getmetians feel like they are kind of limited right now.<br /> <br /> Because they depend so thoroughly on Rakan Thulio, I feel like most of what you're wanting to do with them depends on what you think Rakan Thulio is doing; their Agenda appears to entirely revolve around him, generally working for him though there is one indication of one working against him. Their powers are kind of vague as to what they do, and to me it's not even clear how much free will they really have versus just being Rakan Thulio's personal army.<br /> <br /> In some ways it's kind of freeing, because the answer of 'what is a Getimetian, why are they doing what they are doing, and how do they do it' is basically 'whatever you make up right now.', because it's not clear if Rakan Thulio is using them the way they're supposed to be used or not.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T21:54:23-07:00","id":1246873,"title":"","content":"Must be the difference in culture as my brain has been bubbling with possibilities!<br /> <br /> - 100 Immortals vs 100 Asuras : Who is the TRUE master of Prismatic Rearrangement of Creation Style. The Ultimate Heterodox vs Orthodox sect battle royale!<br /> <br /> - Friends in the Shadow: Chejop Kejak killed my wife and three kids and... oh you want to see his head on a pike too, interesting... Lunars and Gentimians team up to fight the Shadow War!<br /> <br /> - Return of the King! (Out with the old Vizier in with the New Vizier) Now the returned Solar god-Kings don\u2019t have to go to the back stabbing Sids for their Kung Fu sage advice! A new Creation where one Makes their own Fate! (Replace the deebs with the Liminals while you\u2019re at it)<br /> <br /> - 108 (-8) Stars of Destiny! The Turning of the Great Wheel and the Overthrow of the Heavens needs things to be nudged just... so, can you the bearer of a nascent genesis tear down the corrupt system of Chejop Kejak?!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 08-17-2018, 01:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T22:25:19-07:00","id":1246880,"title":"","content":"Daoist sage vs Shinto priest is the aesthetic dynamic at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T22:28:01-07:00","id":1246881,"title":"","content":"With the incredible restraint 3rd edition has had for other realm intereferences running amokin Creation (Heaven &amp; Hell both), and hopefully going to run them more standalone style like Autocthonia, i would say treat them like a Sidereal but their powers open up chance rather lock it down.<br /> <br /> Assuming Sidereals can trade in dice or motes for successes, maybe have a high risk effect with Getimians. Double 9s but subtract successes for 2s. Or add dice but raise the difficulty by a slight amount.<br /> <br /> Keep them and Sidereals as subtle as possible is my primary thought. The less they directly interact with PCs, the less rules they need. The area got its fate cut, so some things act odd here. PCs get attached. Reveal they can 'fix' the area, but does reattaching fate lead to a rise or ruin of the region ( looking at you Lookshy!)? Fun story Getimian themed, but they may have just passed by and left","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24220-cryo-seraph","name":"Cryo-Seraph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-16T22:34:36-07:00","id":1246884,"title":"","content":"This may sound strange but after reading up on them and learning how they work these guys are probably pretty interesting to me.... then again I am assuming its because I am a fan of nocturnals and find the concept of a person wielding quantum physics and fates that could happen fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":893,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","user":"reaperfrost8","date":". 08-17-2018, 01:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T00:30:19-07:00","id":1246898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1246872#post1246872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">they depend so thoroughly on Rakan Thulio</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you basing that on?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T02:38:11-07:00","id":1246930,"title":"","content":"Just like not all Lunars are part of the Silver Pact, or even all Dragon-bloods are part of the Realm, not all Getimians are allied with Rakan Thulio.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T03:25:18-07:00","id":1246944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them#post1246864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's an entire splat that we have no information on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we have some information, if not a lot that came from the core book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do they do?</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to say that they'll have a system of personal and peripheral mote pools being the same size, with Charms having different effects depending on which pool you use to fuel them, but I have a vague sense that the new developers may have said that they found some of that to be mechanically unwieldy and dropped it. They'll still have monochrome anima banners, though.<br /> <br /> As for the agenda, probably something to do with finding life under Heaven being subordinated to the gods and Destiny being distinctly unjust, and working to tear down the old cosmic order.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What <i>can </i>they do, other than hate the Sidereals</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Sidereal Martial Arts, for one. Apparently the idea is something like each one carrying around a personal Fate engine, and powers based on substituting conventional rules of reality in favour of their own. There was an idea once about creating a foot bridge through the air for themselves by a manipulation of gravity to suspend falling debris.<br /> <br /> I'd say that a most basic description of their powers would be similar themes to Sidereal Exalted, but without being bound to fulfil the principles of the Maidens, the alternating aspects of their two-toned mote pools, and the fact that they'll be Attribute Exalted (which would mean losing some of the focused specificity that Sidereals have, but also maybe liberate them to something more free-form; like, a general reality warping ethos might be easier to implement when it doesn't have to be expressed through particular Ability. Consider how Lunars now get something like a Strength Charm to afflict somebody with a terrifying nightmare.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">like that the Lunars also hate the Sidereals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they may like that part, but they might also dislike Lunars in general because they keep going around looning it up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our current idea of their powers, themes and agenda is so vague, I don't even know where to start making things up.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I think that's pretty standard about a thing that's not been written yet. I wouldn't know personally, I have never before been part of Exalted at a time when there were Exalted that people didn't know what they were.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T04:09:56-07:00","id":1246951,"title":"","content":"I think vance said it was looking more like getimians wouldn't be attribute based recently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T04:33:12-07:00","id":1246957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1246880#post1246880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Daoist sage vs Shinto priest is the aesthetic dynamic at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>&gt; Sees a hazy image and intrigued by what might be in the details.<br /> <br /> &quot;Enhance!&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T04:33:44-07:00","id":1246958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1246898#post1246898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are you basing that on?</div> </div> </div> </div> Don't know how much of that still stands, but...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hatewheel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Getimians are puppets\u2014a big part of the Getimian experience is whether the player can cut the strings. That's not something that should happen at character creation, as with Abyssals who go renegade before the game ever begins. With Getimians, self-discovery and the formation of opinions greater than those imparted by Rakan Thulio are a big part of the story, so to reject them outright is to rush past one of the core elements of gameplay. I say all this because the Getimians don't have a uniform feeling about the other Exalted. They only have what Thulio has given them. Individual Getimians forming opinions on the other Exalted is a matter of individual character development and not for me to say. Whereas Liminal views on the other Exalted come on the level of observers who have been around for awhile, it doesn't work for Getimians because they are mostly new.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T05:05:17-07:00","id":1246965,"title":"","content":"All right then; that assumption seems reasonable, although I would argue that the subject has nuances that were not being credited.<br /> <br /> Just if we were discussing things from that old quote, even if it doesn't apply directly anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T06:25:09-07:00","id":1246990,"title":"","content":"What they will do is *definitely* the most interesting and important question about Getimians, and is where I'm still not too clear.<br /> <br /> (Their actual powers as described tend to strike me as like Sidereals, only more disruptive and severing, and less integrative and building, and organised along different themes than those of the Five Maidens. That's reasonably cool but the hook is a bit more in the integration for me much more than this giving rise to immediately striking images and ideas.). <br /> <br /> I tend to think that the experience of playing a Getimian will be some balance between:<br /> <br /> - The local: Being based on a particular locale in Creation and trying to use your powers to effect change there or take hold of power, and to pursue your own personal aims in regards to the culture you come from and the rivalries. <br /> <br /> This is in the bailiwick of what the Solars and Lunars do, where they are playing a person who is a Culture Hero or Great Person within a culture who is trying to do mighty deeds, reverse past injustices to their people or even completely breaking away from this towards more selfish ends that nevertheless (even without intending to) are on a grand scale to become dominant and transformative to the environment they are from / in. Ultimately, this is as part of circle which will be forming a new overarching vision of how the world will work in a region, which will contradict and be on a collision course with the Realm's system.<br /> <br /> - The global: Acting as an agent for Thulio's &quot;War Against Heaven&quot;, where this is more of a globetrotting, intrigue based scenario of cultivating alliances, selling information, organising betrayals and assassinations, acquiring magical assets, building up your network of allies and interests into a form that can take decisive action against Heaven and the Sidereals. <br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> But! for both of these, yeah, I do have some difficulty seeing how the Getimians do either.<br /> <br /> In the case of the former, with their strange and individualistic powers that would alienate them from a culture or at least not serve so well to place them in any position of authority, their thinness on the ground and lack of context, support and well, interest, from most of the established powers of Creation (unlike the Lunars or Solars).<br /> <br /> In the case of the latter, I don't have a good sense of who would be both interested and able to be cultivated as allies in a War Against Heaven - the world doesn't know about the Sidereals, and most of the players who would have an interest in being against Heaven tend to have their own established support bases (Hell, the Underworld, the Fae, maybe the Lunar Exalted) and represent extremely dangerous, pretty unsympathetic allies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T09:25:04-07:00","id":1247046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1246965#post1246965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All right then; that assumption seems reasonable, although I would argue that the subject has nuances that were not being credited.<br /> <br /> Just if we were discussing things from that old quote, even if it doesn't apply directly anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, that does lay it out pretty clearly and we haven't had anything that changes that; a Getimian is defined, at least at the start, by Rakan Thulio and his goals, and either they're advancing his plans or have cut from his plan and are no longer advancing it. If you're following the book/word of Wheel you can't really do anything with them until you know what Rakan Thulio is doing.<br /> <br /> Actually the whole 'if the player can cut the strings' makes me think it may be even harder then I thought it was to get away from Thulio, especially if it's harder then becoming a Renegade Abyssal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T10:02:19-07:00","id":1247056,"title":"","content":"It's hard to just throw out information that hasn't been categorically declared obsolete when we're still this far from a complete picture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T10:33:14-07:00","id":1247069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1247046#post1247046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, that does lay it out pretty clearly and we haven't had anything that changes that; a Getimian is defined, at least at the start, by Rakan Thulio and his goals, and either they're advancing his plans or have cut from his plan and are no longer advancing it. If you're following the book/word of Wheel you can't really do anything with them until you know what Rakan Thulio is doing.<br /> <br /> Actually the whole 'if the player can cut the strings' makes me think it may be even harder then I thought it was to get away from Thulio, especially if it's harder then becoming a Renegade Abyssal.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might be a bit pedantic and doubling down, but I would find that referring to the Getimian Exalted as being on strings is not being directly connected to Rakan Thulio there; the only things attributed directly to him are &quot;opinions&quot;, and perspectives on the other Exalted.<br /> <br /> Given other references to Getimians, such as the original in the Kickstarter and a few sample character concepts, I would have to imagine that part of the Getimian experience involves an actual grievance with Heaven in their own right. I speculate that the main thing that Thulio provides is some context and direction for that; they're already people that have been wronged by Destiny and Rakan, an extremely powerful man that regards himself as also having been wronged by Destiny, comes along to say that Yu-Shan is to blame and that they should share in his rebellion against it. There might be Getimians that decide that they want to defy Heaven on their own terms rather than for Thulio's sake, in addition to ones who decide to get over whatever Destiny did to them, and just wield their power in pursuit of new dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T22:16:58-07:00","id":1247287,"title":"","content":"My only problem with them is that they were started/created/whateverthefuck'ed by an incel.<br /> <br /> I mean, that's flippant as shit, but I cannot get over the fact that Rakan started all this shit because his love chose another person. Like, really dude? You're gonna flip your shit and go &quot;FUCK FATE RAAAAAAAAAAAHHHHH&quot; because Fate didn't drop a hot dude in your lap? This dude is literally &quot;tfw no bf ;__;&quot;, the Sidereal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4801,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","user":"Frostav","date":". 08-18-2018, 01:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-17T22:46:11-07:00","id":1247289,"title":"","content":"Thulio blamed having the hot dude <i>knocked off of </i>his lap on destiny-meddling shenanigans by the Celestial Beaurocracy. Which is either egotistical or insightful.<br /> <br /> <sub><sup>Tale of Visiting Flare adds another take on Thulio's obsession...</sup></sub>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 08-18-2018, 02:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T02:27:11-07:00","id":1247316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1247287#post1247287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only problem with them is that they were started/created/whateverthefuck'ed</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be most accurate to say that they were rediscovered and are being taught and led by him.<br /> <br /> As for the rest, while I would gather that a lot of people in the Exalted fandom actually do have a low opinion of ancient mythology and the literature that derives therein, the idea of grandiose defiance of the natural order over a wounded heart has a lot of artistic pedigree.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T03:12:24-07:00","id":1247321,"title":"","content":"I mean, I get that talking about &quot;incel&quot; is trendy at the moment and its tempting to randomly wedge whatever is trendy into our discussions (no big deal), but really, there's a whole range of modern day scenarios where people can become generally opposed to the government functions in extreme ways because they wreck their private life in what seems to be a cavalier and unnecessary fashion. <br /> <br /> Like, if you responded to &quot;I hate the government because they deported / imprisoned / racially segregated me from / killed my wife, for no good reason&quot;, then the response is like &quot;Hah! Incel!&quot; (like you're Nelson Muntz or something)?<br /> <br /> I'd also have to say, comparing to Arms of the Chosen, I don't get the sense that compared to the other First Age characters described, Rakan Thulio is unusually driven by personal passions and close relationships, in both the balance and manner of the err... conversation between those passions with his wider convictions and beliefs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T03:47:44-07:00","id":1247328,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Rakan Thulio's story will be one in which he's been fighting Destiny since he acquired control over his own thread, and discovery of the Getimians escalated that and made it more efficient because he gained access to soldiers who can more effectively fight on those terms, or if it will be that he mostly kept to himself after seizing his own Fate and the Getimians catalysed his convictions by representing an example that people being unjustly screwed over by Destiny was a more widespread problem.<br /> <br /> Or possibly a case that the kinds of people that can become Getimians have always existed, and Rakan has tried to be an advocate for them with limited success, and the importance of discovering and reviving Getimian Exaltation is that he now actually has a means by which such people can be empowered to take their own vengeance and seize their own destinies.<br /> <br /> After all, one take on the idea of puppetry could be that Thulio radicalizing the Getimian Exalted along an ideology of the unjustness of Heaven and the rightness of opposing it is something that he sincerely believes will be helpful to them, and only wants the best for, but it's still directing them into a life of endemic violence and possibly a general experience of hate and anger, which might not be the best thing for many of them. I think there can be a perspective on charismatic leaders in which they're bad when they're insincere and only using people for their own agenda (whether it be a general power grab or the actual ideology without consideration for human costs), but there's something to be said for the idea of a leader who genuinely wants to improve the lives of the people that they're inspiring and organising, while still not critically evaluating the costs of it.<br /> <br /> Overall, I think that there's fertile ground for discussion of the subject, and that we've not yet gotten any detail about Rakan Thulio that is a basis for writing him off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T12:07:25-07:00","id":1247456,"title":"","content":"I think there are issues with how we were introduced to Rakan but his issues are hardly unique.<br /> <br /> For example, it's pretty easy to frame The Mask of Winters as a ridiculous manchild when you know his backstory as Larquen Quen and I doubt any of the other Deathlords would fare much better under similar scrutiny of their motivations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T12:58:23-07:00","id":1247470,"title":"","content":"We're not really going to know much about Getmetians until we get their book. But it seems likely that one purpose behind them is to give alternative / additional characters for Fate-based stories, providing you with a different take on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T13:09:14-07:00","id":1247476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1247287#post1247287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only problem with them is that they were started/created/whateverthefuck'ed by an incel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think this is more of a problem than people are giving it credit for. Part of the issue <i>behind</i> the whole incel thing is that traditionally stories have portrayed excessive fixation in the face of rejection (and finding the &quot;real&quot; reason you were rejected) in this romantic / heroic light. It's only more recently that we've begun to step back and look at that and realize the serious problems with it, both in terms of the stories themselves and what they teach people who take them seriously. The disaffected men you're referring to are often ones who are rejecting that cultural change.<br /> <br /> So Thulio's backstory is a bit awkward in that it's written in that traditional &quot;rage against the heavens for denying me my love&quot; thing, whereas most modern-day readers are going to stop and say &quot;wait, no, this guy rejected you. Accept it and move on.&quot; And to the extent that it's about fate, it's sort of picking at the scab of free will and the issues players are already going to have with those themes - ie. either Thulio's lover had free will, in which case his story makes him look like a worthless loser who deserves the laughed off the stage, or he didn't, in which case... the entire setting comes into question. Even if you thread the needle and say &quot;well, Thulio's lover was <i>mind-controlled</i> by heaven shenanigans, so they weren't rejecting him of their own free will!&quot;, it leads to serious problems - I'm not really OK with the implications of a story like that.<br /> <br /> If he was a minor side-character this wouldn't be a problem. Picking at cultural or narrative scabs, so to speak, can <i>sometimes</i> be a good thing, and if he was a minor side character an audience reaction of &quot;he's a worthless shitlord whose 'concerns' are total crap&quot; wouldn't necessarily be a bad thing - he could even be seen as a deconstruction of that sort of romantic story, making him as a skeevy monster who doesn't want to accept he was rejected. With characters like that you can also take the risk that your story won't click with some readers, or won't be read the way you intend it to. But as the head of an entire faction, that isn't an option - the game seems to be trying to insist that his story has some grandeur or depth to it, and I suspect a lot of players are going to hard pass on that.<br /> <br /> Basically, a lot of readers are going to have <i>zero</i> patience for any attempt to portray Thulio's story as sympathetic or as anything but a story of how broken this loser is, and that makes him pretty hard to use as a faction leader who needs to have depth and multiple facets. Making such an unsympathic story (and one with such unfortunate implications when viewed in light of real life) central to the main example the game seems to be using for raging against Fate and the heavens seems like a really bad move.<br /> <br /> I suspect that <i>some</i> of this reaction is intentional, but that the authors misjudged the intensity or firmness with which many people are going to... basically, view it as non-heroic, is I think the best way to put it. Thulio comes across as pathetically grasping at straws after a failed relationship, in a way reminiscent of far too many problems in the real world. And once that real-world connection is made, it's going to be very hard to slot him back into a heroic fantasy role in people's minds. Sort of how the Games of Divinity started to lose their grandeur once people view it as a Cosmic X-Box. There isn't really any going back from that - all you can do is tone it down and focus on stuff that works with the audience instead.<br /> <br /> Basically, if I were writing the books, I would nix the story of Thulio's lover <i>hard</i> and it would never appear or be referenced again - I'd come up with some other motivation if necessary (technically an <i>additional</i> motivation, since the lover was mentioned in the core, but only in passing, so it's easy enough to explain as a minor bit of backstory trivia that never came up again, even if that obviously wasn't the original intent.) It's not something that is worth potentially poisoning people's views of Getimians over. Will some people be fine with it? Sure, but the fact that it keeps coming up shows that it's at best an unwelcome distraction.<br /> <br /> (Another option would be to have his lover die, but this would flatly contradict the core.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 08-18-2018, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T14:57:54-07:00","id":1247512,"title":"","content":"I personally don't care about Thulio but if Gementians get used in any game I might run. They'll be done as an extremely powerful created race. That are essentially the goa'uld. I don't think we need more exalted. It just lessens the act of their creation. I also just find alternate races some of which can rival exalts more interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T16:09:01-07:00","id":1247536,"title":"","content":"Yeah I think Thulio's supposed to be viewed as a bit of an asshole.<br /> I remember a few years ago when I talked to John about the Getimians (specifically in the context of how they were different from fanworks such as the Nocturnals) and he made a point about how a dedicated anti-fate faction needs to be a bit unsavoury otherwise the Sidereals end up as <i>their</i> antagonists rather than the other way around.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T16:15:08-07:00","id":1247540,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1247476#post1247476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> either Thulio's lover had free will, in which case his story makes him look like a worthless loser who deserves the laughed off the stage, or he didn't, in which case... the entire setting comes into question.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That's a false dichotomy.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The Dragon Blooded Charm to initiate into sorcery has a number of prerequisites, which Robert has explicitly said is to prevent people from approaching sorcery as so easy and incredibly useful that it's mandatory. That doesn't mean that every player who specifically doesn't take sorcery because they can't be bothered with four other Occult Charms has no free will.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That being said, Shun the Smiling Lady is a Sidereal Charm. It is such an iconic Sidereal Charm that I cannot imagine it being dropped. The existence of the Charm kind of implies that the Bureau of Destiny has a vested interest in curating the romantic relationships of some people. They may or may not have employed that particular Charm (although even if they didn't, there's no getting around the fact that the Sidereal Exalted do in fact have a Charm to affect minds that causes romantic relationships to end), but it's still a thing that they do, and it can be as simple as having arranged a meet cute between the Sword Saint and somebody that he would like better than Rakan Thulio.</span></span></span></div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1247512#post1247512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally don't care about Thulio but if Gementians get used in any game I might run. They'll be done as an extremely powerful created race. That are essentially the goa'uld. I don't think we need more exalted. It just lessens the act of their creation. I also just find alternate races some of which can rival exalts more interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't speak for anybody else, but I can assure you, your absence was not long enough for me to forget you bringing up variations of this point every five posts or so.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T16:42:24-07:00","id":1247545,"title":"","content":"Similar things less succinctly and well than Levi:<br /> <br /> I'm not sure our ideas about love have changed that much. Or at least, I hope, as a culture, our capacity to deal with the human experience of heartbreak and take it seriously and sympathetically and to understand how even great people can be profoundly affected by it, has not been reduced and coarsened that much. (My read of pop culture has not been that people are suddenly blase about heartbreak, and unsympathetic to people who remain attached after their relationships break down, but I could be deeply wrong.)<br /> <br /> On a more specific level to the audience for this game, historically (and perhaps human experience pre-2017 is almost irrelevant to today's reality, and society has completely changed in a very short space of time) the audience for Exalted has not really had a problem with the idea that Heaven can and does break people's love lives, and that them doing this both doesn't detonate the setting and is still Heaven's responsibility. <br /> <br /> (Like, &quot;I use Shun The Smiling Lady on the target!&quot; equals the audience enthusiastically agreeing &quot;Get over it!&quot; towards the target? Indeed, the objections usually tended to be that this is overpowered and not fair to be able to target a PC! Not that it ever broke the setting or that targets should just brush it off emotionally as &quot;He's just not that into you&quot;.)<br /> <br /> I'd also say, to use a more general case, we know that the Sidereals engage in complex interventions into Fate, to achieve a given ends, without stripping people of their free will. If a Sidereal really did engage in one of these complex interventions to say, strip a person of their kingdom and raise another in their place, would we then be sitting there going &quot;Well, everyone still had free will, so..... I can't even sympathize with your rage against Heaven&quot;? Or take another example, perhaps of a woman who had been stripped of the love of her beloved child by the machinations of a Heaven that intended to set her down a more useful path? If not, why does romance become something different?<br /> <br /> But, really, this is all in the realms of &quot;I do/don't think people at large would think this way&quot;. This seems mostly like a sort of a useless thing to argue about, as anyone involved in the conversation can simply flatly declare how &quot;society&quot; or &quot;the audience&quot; would react and we have no way of breaking deadlock and going further with that conversation. None of us can really own or prove what we might believe about how &quot;the audience&quot; would react. (Or if the authors should even care that some people will have bad ideas that will stop them clicking with what they present!) Unlike simply exchanging on our personal views and experiences, or on the text or rules, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T16:46:24-07:00","id":1247548,"title":"","content":"Oh, it was mentioned I believe that they have equal peripheral and personal pools, and I remember the impression that which fueled their charms effected the charms abillities.<br /> <br /> Thulio's story fits the mode of &quot;lover scorned seeks revenege&quot; which I think was supposed to be troubling at best. It might be better pitched as &quot;Thulio started rethinking Destiny when it screwed him over&quot;--'screwed him over' being specifically perventing him from pursuing his love-- and give the Getmetians some more meaty thoughts later from his reflections. Certainly, second thoughts regarding a system or plan or organization that interfered with your personal life is not <i>impossible</i>. There are I think substantial enough differences between Thulio's rage against the machine with his sidereal allies and the current crop of--no, not the time and place for that. I don't think the Incel comparison is valid, and I'm pretty sure Gets will have good or at least understandable reasons.<br /> <br /> More important for Getmetians and Sids is how Fate works--an intreasting concept for Getmetians to me is that they overlap or override local activities of Fate in...less constructive ways then sidereals. To use a bad analogy--Sidereals are people with the Admin tools for fate around them, Getmetians are the ones that hacked the system. Or Sidereals are james bond, backed by a vast government machine that employs them around the world to secure things--Getmetians are the folks who made their tools in a garage and are on the move, rebels and insurgents who have to use their own network built from scratch to deal with their opponent.<br /> <br /> The Taoist vs Shinto perspective I think implies similiar things. At the end of the day, Sidereals are secret agents, bueracrats(not in the sense of modern connotations, where they are fewed as obstructive, but in the sense of being proffessionals overseeing the operations of a government), and more. Getmetians, even when they work in Heaven (and there was one that worked for Heaven if I recall correctly) are consultants at best and more likely to be sages and mystics and rebels who make their own power.<br /> <br /> I don't imagine, in otherwords, Getmetians have much use for prayer strips.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":11835,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","user":"Epee102","date":". 08-18-2018, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T17:05:55-07:00","id":1247550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1247545#post1247545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similar things less succinctly and well than Levi:<br /> <br /> I'm not sure our ideas about love have changed that much. Or at least, I hope, as a culture, our capacity to deal with the human experience of heartbreak and take it seriously and sympathetically and to understand how even great people can be profoundly affected by it, has not been reduced and coarsened that much. (My read of pop culture has not been that people are suddenly blase about heartbreak, and unsympathetic to people who remain attached after their relationships break down, but I could be deeply wrong.).</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I see it, there is a difference between Heartbreak and what Rakan Thulio is doing.<br /> <br /> When I think Heartbreak, I think two people who love each other but can't be together because they're like Oil and Water, or who were in love once but have fallen apart, someone who loves someone but, through either their sin or their partners, have broken their trust and their relationship. Things that represent a long period of investment only to be turned down or put away, and how they react to that. That's sad. It's sad when two people cared for each other and don't anymore, or someone cares for someone but they can't be together.<br /> <br /> I don't think 'I liked this guy then it turns out he had a boyfriend, and that's a betrayal to ME.'. That's not sympathetic. Getting turned down for a date and responding by writing screeds about how Chad took your Stacey and you're gonna kill all the Chads is not sympathetic, because it's a difference between putting forth effort and trying and thinking that you deserve it. Rakan Thulio doesn't come across as someone who broke up with a guy he liked because they couldn't be together, or someone who fell apart because of intense disagreements. He comes across as a guy who found someone he thought was cute and for various reasons that person was not available. If you take the comic as canon, he responded to his by actually having that guy murdered, because if he couldn't have him, no one could have him.<br /> <br /> And part of this is that it's been about 3 years since his introduction and we still don't really know anything about him. Maybe there was more then what it seems, but right now we have what we have, and that's him being the same kind of person that we now see a lot of, saying they 'deserve' a relationship.<br /> <br /> another point of it; for all those examples of Heartbreak, when I think of them, it also involves self-reflection on where you went wrong as a person, where you fucked things up. Rakan Thulio isn't reflecting on his failures, he places the blame entirely on what he sees as an unjust system of Fate and that the only way to rectify it is to tear it all down. And the Sword Saint is never shown as reciprocating Thulio's feelings, which adds another layer to it; Thulio isn't shown fighting against a fate that broke his relationship with his loved one, he's fighting against a Fate of 'hey, that guy doesn't like you like that' and he's going 'THAT ISN'T FAIR!'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T17:13:00-07:00","id":1247553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1247545#post1247545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(My read of pop culture has not been that people are suddenly blase about heartbreak, and unsympathetic to people who remain attached after their relationships break down, but I could be deeply wrong.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The last I checked, The Phantom of the Opera was still tremendously popular.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, today I happened upon some information about Arthurian literature that introduced me to the character of Galahaut (not to be confused with Galahad), a rebel lord with great power, charisma and legions of loyal followers, whose rebellion against the king is stopped not by any kind of military loss, but because he's so impressed by the battlefield skill and valour of Lancelot that he's willing to submit himself to the other knight's liege. My read was obviously limited, but it came across to me as though the two men's epic bromance had a pivotal role in Lancelot's affair with Guinevere, in the sense that Galahaut had to kind of let Lancelot out of the conditions of their own relationship so that he could be free to pursue his lady love, crossed over with a sense that Lancelot could only really do it (it being a violation of his own fidelity to his king and his lover's marriage vows) when he had the blessing of the closest man in his life.<br /> <br /> Leaving aside all of the fascinating implications of that as a piece of Medieval literature in terms of perceptions of gendered relationships and variations within chivalric romance, there's a lot of fun epic melodrama in there, I think.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T17:19:42-07:00","id":1247555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1247540#post1247540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't speak for anybody else, but I can assure you, your absence was not long enough for me to forget you bringing up variations of this point every five posts or so.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>This got flagged for rudeness so I'm going to nip this in the bud,<br /> Top Right Icon &gt; User Profile &gt; Edit Settings &gt; Account &gt; Ignore List<br /> It's what I did and the browsing experience is far more pleasurable. </b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T17:24:22-07:00","id":1247557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1247550#post1247550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't think 'I liked this guy then it turns out he had a boyfriend, and that's a betrayal to ME.'</div> </div> </div> </div>You must know that this is not a thing that the book says, right?<br /> <br /> I mean, all of this (gestures at the entire rest of the post}, this is you reading <i><b>way</b></i> into things, in the most uncharitable light possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And part of this is that it's been about 3 years since his introduction and we still don't really know anything about him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Until a few months ago, that went for everything about the Dragon Blooded as well. The delay has been bad all round, and does not reflect on the specific elements that any given person happens to not like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">another point of it; for all those examples of Heartbreak, when I think of them, it also involves self-reflection on where you went wrong as a person, where you fucked things up. Rakan Thulio isn't reflecting on his failures, he places the blame entirely on what he sees as an unjust system of Fate and that the only way to rectify it is to tear it all down.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be a more compelling argument in the absence of an unjust system of Fate.<br /> <br /> Jesus, people used to be up in arms about the constellation of the Lovers, but now we're going to act like it doesn't exist? Like it doesn't matter? Sure, fine, we don't know if it specifically will (even though I'm confident that Robert Vance is enough of an admirer of everything that Sidereals have always been as to make its absence unlikely), but it serves as a precedent to form the basis of credible arguments, and I'm surprised to find some people here, some of whom I have known to be part of the community for quite some time, suddenly forgetting about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the Sword Saint is never shown as reciprocating Thulio's feelings</div> </div> </div> </div>He's never shown doing much of anything, least of all anything that didn't have to do with swords.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T17:51:25-07:00","id":1247565,"title":"","content":"I... I'm going to stop. I don't like what I am in these last couple of threads; what I'm encouraging myself to be. It's awful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T18:18:32-07:00","id":1247569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1247540#post1247540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't speak for anybody else, but I can assure you, your absence was not long enough for me to forget you bringing up variations of this point every five posts or so.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been at least over a year and it's not even your thread so I don't know why you're being so confrontational about this.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T18:21:34-07:00","id":1247571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1247557#post1247557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You must know that this is not a thing that the book says, right?<br /> <br /> I mean, all of this (gestures at the entire rest of the post}, this is you reading <i><b>way</b></i> into things, in the most uncharitable light possible.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, we know that his war on heaven is beacuse his love was denied. It doesn't make it sound like there was a relationship.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1247557#post1247557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Until a few months ago, that went for everything about the Dragon Blooded as well. The delay has been bad all round, and does not reflect on the specific elements that any given person happens to not like.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This is still a valid response when someone asks 'what do I do with Getimians' and they're intrinsically linked to someone that is trying to be set up as one of the Setting's new Big Bads. It's like saying 'how do I use Infernals' and saying 'well don't worry about the Yozi'; you kinda have to care about Rakan Thulio unless you're just gonna use Getimiens as some guest star in a story where they're doing it for some vague and unexplained plan that doesn't actually exist.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1247557#post1247557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This would be a more compelling argument in the absence of an unjust system of Fate.<br /> <br /> Jesus, people used to be up in arms about the constellation of the Lovers, but now we're going to act like it doesn't exist? Like it doesn't matter? Sure, fine, we don't know if it specifically will (even though I'm confident that Robert Vance is enough of an admirer of everything that Sidereals have always been as to make its absence unlikely), but it serves as a precedent to form the basis of credible arguments, and I'm surprised to find some people here, some of whom I have known to be part of the community for quite some time, suddenly forgetting about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>'Fate is inherently unjust' is probably not a good 100% true face for the setting to have so long as Sidereals are at least vaguely presented as heroic. I'm certainly fine with there being problems with it, and even the idea that sometimes people get lost in the cracks and forgotten and that being where Getimiens come from or something like that. Claiming Fate is innately unjust hits the same thing Lioness was talking about earlier where the Sidereals can easily become the villains. And to be honest, for me as a person; I've never played a Sidereal (I'm playing a person who will eventually Exalt as one, though), but even like that I can tell that making a splat that was something that people liked into the antagonists for a new splat isn't a great idea. Even if Fate IS inherently unjust, I still think there's better champions for it, like the actual people who got fucked over by Fate so hard they Exalted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1247557#post1247557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's never shown doing much of anything, least of all anything that didn't have to do with swords.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe he should have, if just to help Thulio's story.<br /> <br /> EDIT: This went up before your post showed up. I respect that and won't pester you further.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":108,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","user":"Flare","date":". 08-18-2018, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T20:01:03-07:00","id":1247589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1247571#post1247571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'Fate is inherently unjust' is probably not a good 100% true face for the setting to have so long as Sidereals are at least vaguely presented as heroic. I'm certainly fine with there being problems with it, and even the idea that sometimes people get lost in the cracks and forgotten and that being where Getimiens come from or something like that. Claiming Fate is innately unjust hits the same thing Lioness was talking about earlier where the Sidereals can easily become the villains. And to be honest, for me as a person; I've never played a Sidereal (I'm playing a person who will eventually Exalt as one, though), but even like that I can tell that making a splat that was something that people liked into the antagonists for a new splat isn't a great idea. Even if Fate IS inherently unjust, I still think there's better champions for it, like the actual people who got fucked over by Fate so hard they Exalted.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Fate inherently is what it is. Sometimes it's just. Sometimes it's unjust. A lot of what sidereals do can screw good men and women for the greater good. It can also uplift people. It's inherently fickle and are represented by the maidens. A lot of the maiden's have negative as well as positive traits. My real problem with getimians comes from the fact that fate is dictated by the loom. Damaging and destroying it, destroys creation as a whole. Paradoxes lead to events where demons escape hell, shadowlands are formed and the fairfolk can turn areas of creation back into the wyld. Unless there's a significant change in the loom and fate this edition, Getimians are a threat to everything in creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T20:10:35-07:00","id":1247592,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1247589#post1247589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fate inherently is what it is. Sometimes it's just. Sometimes it's unjust. A lot of what sidereals do can screw good men and women for the greater good. It can also uplift people. It's inherently fickle and are represented by the maidens. A lot of the maiden's have negative as well as positive traits. My real problem with getimians comes from the fact that fate is dictated by the loom. Damaging and destroying it, destroys creation as a whole. Paradoxes lead to events where demons escape hell, shadowlands are formed and the fairfolk can turn areas of creation back into the wyld. Unless there's a significant change in the loom and fate this edition, Getimians are a threat to everything in creation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Unless Rakan doesn't believe that the loom is as necessary to Creation as is believed, or believes that there's an alternate method. Afterall even without Sidereal, or even exalt, interference events in Creation do not always play out the way things are dictated by the loom. Entirely possible for a bitter Rakan to come to the conclusion that the purpose of the loom is to manipulate and that he and the Sids are merely being fooled into being the catspaws of whatever mad game he thinks the Maidens are running. Even if he doesn't believe that, he's the expert so it wouldn't be that hard for the Getimians to be under the impression that such is the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T20:38:21-07:00","id":1247601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1247592#post1247592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Unless Rakan doesn't believe that the loom is as necessary to Creation as is believed, or believes that there's an alternate method. Afterall even without Sidereal, or even exalt, interference events in Creation do not always play out the way things are dictated by the loom. Entirely possible for a bitter Rakan to come to the conclusion that the purpose of the loom is to manipulate and that he and the Sids are merely being fooled into being the catspaws of whatever mad game he thinks the Maidens are running. Even if he doesn't believe that, he's the expert so it wouldn't be that hard for the Getimians to be under the impression that such is the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose that's possible that he has an alternative but the loom has always been stated to be what holds creation together. That's been a staple in every edition. Maybe he thinks the damages are manageable.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T21:01:46-07:00","id":1247606,"title":"","content":"I wonder if the Getimians, being pseudo looms themselves are what he imagines to base Creation on after cracking the one in Heaven?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T21:06:30-07:00","id":1247607,"title":"","content":"I don't believe Thulio's been described as intending to destroy the Loom of Fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T21:06:55-07:00","id":1247608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1247601#post1247601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose that's possible that he has an alternative but the loom has always been stated to be what holds creation together. That's been a staple in every edition. Maybe he thinks the damages are manageable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> the Core mentions that Rakan has convinced Sids to help in the past. I suspect that he has an alternative planned, or that the Loom isn't as neccessary, or perhaps even that he's more concerned with who controls the Loom then the Loom itself (It's a War in/with Heaven not Fate).<br /> EDIT:<br /> Also, the Gets are, IIRC, new to the War. Rakan's goal couldn't have been &quot;replace the Loom with Getmetians as a decenteralized form of fate weaving&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T21:32:44-07:00","id":1247609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1247607#post1247607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't believe Thulio's been described as intending to destroy the Loom of Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose the extent of the damage will have to be detailed in the core book but everything about them seems to effect the loom negatively right now.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-18T22:38:37-07:00","id":1247619,"title":"","content":"Hmm the Loom would be a major target even if one had no plans to destroy or mess with it. I mean even taking the tendency for Exalts to not be effected by their own fates the Loom would still represent an exceptional amount of information that could be leveraged for a lot of different goals. I mean lets go with a base assumption that the Gets view the Realm as an enemy for the sole reason that it is a powerful asset/ally the Sidereal have. (No evidence, just postulation here.) If you wanted to screw up the Realm the Loom would tell you the most likely points where it could be vulnerable, or tipping off individuals that might be interested in the future events. Just, &quot;Some of my associates have noticed a number an uptick in stories and information crossing a few desks in Memnom and Peleps recently. Looked like there might be some plans for something going on and judging by some of the arrangements I wouldn't expect any of them to move before winter. Thought that might be of interest to you.&quot; Just as an attempt to get someone looking in the right direction to take actions or the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T02:03:20-07:00","id":1247644,"title":"","content":"At this point, I kinda feel like we just don\u2019t really have enough info about them to really involve them in a game. I mean, yes, we do know more about them than we do about Hearteaters or The Spoken, but without even a sample QC or a \u201cprestige spread\u201d like the various exalt types got in the Core, it\u2019s hard to get enough of an idea what they\u2019ll be like to actually use them. <br /> <br /> At least for me anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T03:15:36-07:00","id":1247654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1247550#post1247550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The way I see it, there is a difference between Heartbreak and what Rakan Thulio is doing.<br /> <br /> When I think Heartbreak, I think two people who love each other but can't be together because they're like Oil and Water, or who were in love once but have fallen apart, someone who loves someone but, through either their sin or their partners, have broken their trust and their relationship. Things that represent a long period of investment only to be turned down or put away, and how they react to that. That's sad. It's sad when two people cared for each other and don't anymore, or someone cares for someone but they can't be together.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the only thing we have really is: &quot;But when the love of his life chose another, he came to believe that Heaven had done him a great injustice.&quot; I would interpret that these two men were lovers, and then his lover &quot;chose another&quot;. But as you say, open season on interpretation.<br /> <br /> Though will say, heartbreak is not just because of people who are in love, but find the relationship doesn't really work. Sometimes one of you falls *out* of love, or falls for someone else harder, while the other remains attached. (Like this sounds patronising as I think you know this right? But the guy/girl, I'm quoting doesn't seem to, from, what I'm quoting).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1247550#post1247550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think 'I liked this guy then it turns out he had a boyfriend, and that's a betrayal to ME.'. That's not sympathetic. Getting turned down for a date and responding by writing screeds about how Chad took your Stacey and you're gonna kill all the Chads is not sympathetic, because it's a difference between putting forth effort and trying and thinking that you deserve it. Rakan Thulio doesn't come across as someone who broke up with a guy he liked because they couldn't be together, or someone who fell apart because of intense disagreements</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's really a case of anything that can be analogous to that, or conversely, a &quot;That handsome, successful guy doesn't seem interested in me... it's because society is wrong about what makes women attractive, the ideals it presents, and has such high expectations for women! Bad and toxic social messages must be to blame and I must war against society through activism to create change!&quot; type. If you look at the text, I don't think the analogy really works, and requires assumptions to make it work that I don't think are warranted... or if they were originally what John intended, probably would be a good idea to shift to one of two lovers whose relationship has broken down, yes.<br /> <br /> This is getting kind of a bit peripheral to the argument as well, but as depicted in the art, Thulio is a tall, muscular, handsome, tanned, dark haired man who basically wouldn't look out of place in Jen's art. Add to that what we know from his character, what he'd have to be like to do what he'd has done and he's a charismatic, decisive, powerful, worldly and experienced leader. So I think, while he may voluntarily abstain from romantic relationships, he's probably been able to &quot;get&quot; a lot from other similarly handsome men, over the years and if anything he's a &quot;Chad&quot; (accepting for a millisecond only these foolish, distorting terms with very little value). And that confirms to me that really we should definitely be thinking more of a case that he's lost someone who he loved and not anything to do with general sexual frustration or an inability to form a relationship with anyone at all.<br /> <br /> And of course we may decide that it's sympathetic or unsympathetic, and even if it's not sympathetic, whether Thulio's wider ideology that grew out of this and really drives his actions is still sympathetic. But I do strongly feel we should begin from the point of thinking about love and heartbreak and how those are viewed within our culture (and applying the same standards to men and women and that both genders have the same rights to express and feel!), and not the standpoint of trying to make these analogies with this current vocal subset of young men who are sexually frustrated, can't find anyone to have any sort of romantic relationship with and have adopted some strange and alienated ideas about society because of it (mostly because of almost nothing to with how our culture has for time immemorial viewed heartbreak).<br /> <br /> ....<br /> <br /> Anyway, actually getting back to thread topic, also wanted to chime in that reading the 3e text again did help me on some Getimian related matters: &quot;<i>Rakan Thulio has been at war with Yu-Shan for centuries. He is far from alone. A handful of Sidereals have bolstered his ranks, each with their own reasons to betray Heaven. Collectively, the conspirators bring to bear intimate knowledge of the divine bureaucracies. They\u2019ve turned the political landscape of Yu-Shan into a battleground, and the city itself into the site of a shadow war between those loyal to the Celestial Bureaucracy and those who wish to see it torn down. Dissident and outcast gods flock to his banner; in exchange for their service, Thulio and his allies promise them new roles in the order to come.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> So that resolves part of my original questions about Getimians from my first post in this thread, in that tells me that the Getimians are going to be mixed game OK with Sidereals (with a particular flavour that the Sidereal players get to be double agents) and that part of play is going to be winning dissident gods over on side as allies. Should have read it first!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T10:08:05-07:00","id":1247748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1247654#post1247654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna ignore this point where you quote a post of mine, which specifically states 'people falling out of love' as a condition for heartbreak and it being sad to then turn to the audience and go 'THIS GUY SEEMS TO HAVE MISSED THAT PEOPLE CAN FALL OUT OF LOVE, ISN'T HE A BIT DENSE' because anyone can read my post and see I already brought that up, and even specifically brought it up in the part you quoted, and instead talking about the other parts of this post.<br /> <br /> I think that you should watch more romance movies, because the idea of 'person falls out of love with someone to be with someone else', has been presented from both the side of the person whose lover abandons him and the side of the person who is abandoning their lover, and I feel like right now we're at least in a phase where the second one is more generally given as the viewpoint character. I haven't done any scientific rigor, but I can think of a lot of movies off the top of my head where the climax of the film involves the protagonist or the object of affection leaving someone they've been in a committed relationship with to go be with the person they truly love, and that the person they are already in a relationship with is portrayed generally as an obstacle, though generally not an out and out villain; this does usually have a lot of dramatic soul searching on the part of the person who leaves, because they are the protagonist, but it is not like such a thing is uncommon or never happens, and you can't go 'well society still loves heartbreak and respects it' but ignore that, in a lot of ways, this seems to instead follow the plot of that kind of movie, instead of a more flat 'two people meet each other and slowly learn to be together'. The love of his life choosing another could be sad, but if you're using romance movie tropes on heartbreak, that should inform how it's observed; If Rakan Thulio is left behind because the person he loved didn't love him anymore, then getting a bunch of people to murder that guy is not actually a move of 'oh, he's so sad', it's 'holy shit he's off his rocker.', he's the one standing in the way of True Love, not the guy who has True Love.<br /> <br /> The other thing, to get back onto the topic as you did, is that your idea of using Getimiens is a Mixed Game with Sidereals is 'Okay, so you Sidereals are all rebelling against Heaven', then that might not be the best side for an older splat to go 'okay, actually the new guys are right'. At least as a baseline assumption. Certainly it's something that could be valid, but it probably shouldn't be the only valid possibility or the first one offered.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T10:28:08-07:00","id":1247751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1247654#post1247654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anyway, actually getting back to thread topic, also wanted to chime in that reading the 3e text again did help me on some Getimian related matters: &quot;<i>Rakan Thulio has been at war with Yu-Shan for centuries. He is far from alone. A handful of Sidereals have bolstered his ranks, each with their own reasons to betray Heaven. Collectively, the conspirators bring to bear intimate knowledge of the divine bureaucracies. They\u2019ve turned the political landscape of Yu-Shan into a battleground, and the city itself into the site of a shadow war between those loyal to the Celestial Bureaucracy and those who wish to see it torn down. Dissident and outcast gods flock to his banner; in exchange for their service, Thulio and his allies promise them new roles in the order to come.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> So that resolves part of my original questions about Getimians from my first post in this thread, in that tells me that the Getimians are going to be mixed game OK with Sidereals (with a particular flavour that the Sidereal players get to be double agents) and that part of play is going to be winning dissident gods over on side as allies. Should have read it first!</div> </div> </div> </div>An example Get was a consultant for the Buereu of Destiny as well, so yeah. Turncoats are an option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T12:18:39-07:00","id":1247773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1247748#post1247748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna ignore this point where you quote a post of mine, which specifically states 'people falling out of love' as a condition for heartbreak and it being sad to then turn to the audience and go 'THIS GUY SEEMS TO HAVE MISSED THAT PEOPLE CAN FALL OUT OF LOVE, ISN'T HE A BIT DENSE' because anyone can read my post and see I already brought that up, and even specifically brought it up in the part you quoted, and instead talking about the other parts of this post.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly didn't specifically spot how you were saying that, and it wouldn't make sense for me to have said that if I really did think it were that obvious that it would be obvious to everyone reading. (If I were playing to the gallery, it wouldn't make sense to flatly contradict something that is obvious in your post to all. It would just make me look foolish?). I really did read the quoted section as only allowing for a mutual break down of love or a functional relationship, not a one sided breakdown of love. Apologies if I did miss what you were expressing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1247748#post1247748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that you should watch more romance movies, because the idea of 'person falls out of love with someone to be with someone else', has been presented from both the side of the person whose lover abandons him and the side of the person who is abandoning their lover, and I feel like right now we're at least in a phase where the second one is more generally given as the viewpoint character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, that's a common trope; there was an interesting documentary about tricks of film genres I was watching a few weeks ago, covered the rom com and how this trope evolved within it (<a href=\"https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/b0bbn5x8\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/b0bbn5x8</a>). Most commonly until now with an evolution from the unsympathetic &quot;unsuitable partner&quot; of early genre pieces in the mid 20th century to a more viable partner who usually has their own love interests, even though they are ultimately discarded, in newer pieces. But yeah, I certainly don't think they are, or have ever been the main staple viewpoint character; &quot;100 Days of Summer&quot; is an exception I can think of (I don't know if that's considered a &quot;problematic&quot; movie post-2016). <br /> <br /> That is true for comedies though, and of course they're light and uplifting, serious romantic dramas and tragedies are a bit different, but I can't really say one way or the other how those work out in absolute terms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1247748#post1247748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The love of his life choosing another could be sad, but if you're using romance movie tropes on heartbreak, that should inform how it's observed; If Rakan Thulio is left behind because the person he loved didn't love him anymore, then getting a bunch of people to murder that guy is not actually a move of 'oh, he's so sad', it's 'holy shit he's off his rocker.', he's the one standing in the way of True Love, not the guy who has True Love.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't want you to think I'm accusing you of being dense, but you have to think there's a difference between &quot;Rakan has good reason to believe a shadow government of the world has conspired to destroy his relationship, and he is a senior member of this government and no has ever been able to persuade him differently, that this changed his mind on how widely unjust they are and that they must be brought down&quot;, and something like &quot;Agamemnon's wife Helen fell in love with Paris and Agamemnon is out to raze Paris's Troy to the ground and drive a sword through Paris's heart&quot;? <br /> <br /> There's no indication that Rakan Thulio went off to murder any specific person that he lost his love to (though IRC, after the Usurpation, that may have been a moot point), and instead he directs his energies against a Celestial Bureaucracy that, as I read it, he believes to twist the fates of humanity for the greater good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1247748#post1247748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other thing, to get back onto the topic as you did, is that your idea of using Getimiens is a Mixed Game with Sidereals is 'Okay, so you Sidereals are all rebelling against Heaven', then that might not be the best side for an older splat to go 'okay, actually the new guys are right'. At least as a baseline assumption. Certainly it's something that could be valid, but it probably shouldn't be the only valid possibility or the first one offered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I agree that wouldn't be a good baseline assumption for Sidereals as a whole, but I don't think the book is presenting it as the baseline assumption for Sidereals as a whole, and as Epee notes, there is a reverse example of the Getimian consultant out there as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T13:00:42-07:00","id":1247784,"title":"","content":"You might want to take a look at Ex3 comic 'Tale of the Visiting Flare'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThe very existence of flame-throwers proves that some time, somewhere, someone said to themselves, You know, I want to set those people over there on fire, but I'm just not close enough to get the job done.\u201d George Carlin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/123-trax","name":"Trax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar123_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T14:07:50-07:00","id":1247800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1247784#post1247784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might want to take a look at Ex3 comic 'Tale of the Visiting Flare'.</div> </div> </div> </div>to piggy back off this and explain, I am not talking about a metaphor when I bring up Rakan Thulio killing the person he loved. The Tale of the Visiting Flare is the first piece of Ex3 Media that was ever published, way before the corebook even. In it, a Sidereal lays out that Rakan Thulio killed the Sword Saint by having a bunch of people show up to his house and kill him, specifically saying that he killed him because he felt that no one else could love the Sword saint as much as he did, then for good measure cursed his future incarnations as well. And while the Sidereal could be lying, it would be weird to immediately start the introduction of a main villain with someone badmouthing him in a way that isn't true, and then a few pages later the Solar gets into a fight with a Lunar who specifically calls him the Sword Saint, which means it is probably meant to be indicative that the curse is actually true.<br /> <br /> So no, he didn't murder a specific person. He murdered the guy he loved so no one else could have him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":108,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","user":"Flare","date":". 08-19-2018, 05:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T14:34:40-07:00","id":1247813,"title":"","content":"Hmm... That comic being what it is, yeah, how I read the core is basically invalid, assuming it's true. Though there are reasons to doubt it - the Sidereal sort of elided over the Usurpation in favour of pinning sealing away the protagonists Exaltation purely on Thulio's love. It's not impossible to think of why a Gold Sidereal might want to do that... But I will assume that the comic basically is directly honest and delivers John Morke's vision, and yeah, Thulio is then kind of blatantly hard to sympathize with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T14:37:39-07:00","id":1247815,"title":"","content":"I think it's entirely possible it gets changed at least a little. But it might not, and regardless of what it will be in the future, it is what it is now, so the way I see it, it is something to take into mind. Particularly it doesn't seem like the Sidereal is blaming him for the whole Usurpation, just the murder of the Saint. It depends on what happens, but I'd also not immediately assume the Sidereal was just being a liar, because I think introducing what's supposed to be a huge antagonist and then saying he's actually being unfairly demonized on his very first action could lead to a shift in prospectives.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also there's a question of motives and thoughts in things; Generally it seems like the assumption with the Usurpation is that the Sidereals were doing it because they thought it was the right thing to do. If Thulio was doing it purely because it let him Murder the Saint and seal him away, then regardless of if he did it during the Usurpation or not, he's still not in the right no matter the opinion on the Usurpation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":108,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","user":"Flare","date":". 08-19-2018, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-19T14:57:53-07:00","id":1247819,"title":"","content":"I do kind of wonder why a Sidereal (famously manipulative) simply goes straight to &quot;<i>The Sword Priest was dead and his title slipped away to a jade cage among the stars</i>&quot; *without* mentioning, presumably &quot;And this happened at a time when the Sidereals had chosen kill the Solars en masse, then seal them away to banish their increasing tyranny&quot; (a contextually rather important detail). <br /> <br /> But the straightforward interpretation is the straightforward interpretation, for all the reasons you've given, and though I'd still defend what I've written in this thread, as viable without considering the comic, I'm not going to bat for what is effectively IPV and honor killings as a culturally sympathetic touchstone! (I mean, what would I do for my next trick? &quot;Desus did nothing wrong&quot;? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T07:57:03-07:00","id":1248050,"title":"","content":"Given that one of Thulio's explicit inspirations is Revolver Ocelot, I think it's okay for him to be a mildly ridiculous dude if you handle it right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T08:06:23-07:00","id":1248053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rand Brittain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1248050#post1248050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that one of Thulio's explicit inspirations is Revolver Ocelot, I think it's okay for him to be a mildly ridiculous dude if you handle it right.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Ocelot's an explicit inspiration for Thulio at all!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T08:22:57-07:00","id":1248063,"title":"","content":"Are we assuming that Thulio's love was of the romantic sort, or is that inclusive of other interpretations? <br /> <br /> Have we considered that he might have loved so deeply because he was Solar-brain-whammied into doing so, over and over? (I'd be pretty obsessed and conflicted if I'd been putting up with a few centuries of that, myself.)<br /> <br /> Not so much a question, but I notice that - for the moment - we have a whole <i>Splat: The Upcoming</i> focused on the exploits of one particular guy. That's a pretty distinct difference, in that other splats orbit around their Celestine++ patrons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T10:11:38-07:00","id":1248120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1248063#post1248063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not so much a question, but I notice that - for the moment - we have a whole <i>Splat: The Upcoming</i> focused on the exploits of one particular guy. That's a pretty distinct difference, in that other splats orbit around their Celestine++ patrons.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Getimians have an awesome hook that could make them a fan favourite (it really depends on if Exigents takes or if we get a repeat of Devil Tigers where most of the energy gets spent on telling people they're doing it wrong). It's been heavily hinted at over the years but never stated outright.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T10:33:05-07:00","id":1248127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1248120#post1248120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Getimians have an awesome hook that could make them a fan favourite (it really depends on if Exigents takes or if we get a repeat of Devil Tigers where most of the energy gets spent on telling people they're doing it wrong). It's been heavily hinted at over the years but never stated outright.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it frustrating when you do things like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T10:54:50-07:00","id":1248132,"title":"","content":"Sorry, but it's agonising that a topic about one of the coolest things I was told about for Ex3 ends up as a discussion of Rakan Thulio's sex life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T11:51:01-07:00","id":1248156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1248053#post1248053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Ocelot's an explicit inspiration for Thulio at all!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Once he was! But Creation has many pasts and many masters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine\" target=\"_blank\">Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG</a> \u2014 <a href=\"http://www.patreon.com/JennaMoran\" target=\"_blank\">Jenna Moran's Patreon</a> \u2014 <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/215-rand-brittain","name":"Rand Brittain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar215_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T12:14:56-07:00","id":1248163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1248120#post1248120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Getimians have an awesome hook that could make them a fan favourite (it really depends on if Exigents takes or if we get a repeat of Devil Tigers where most of the energy gets spent on telling people they're doing it wrong). It's been heavily hinted at over the years but never stated outright.</div> </div> </div> </div>I will have to just disagree, they come from a place of &quot;we need rival exalts&quot; which I think is a terrible premise. There could have been a bunch of ways to introduce them but I can't say I enjoyed the way the core introduced them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T12:46:13-07:00","id":1248180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1247536#post1247536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah I think Thulio's supposed to be viewed as a bit of an asshole.<br /> I remember a few years ago when I talked to John about the Getimians (specifically in the context of how they were different from fanworks such as the Nocturnals) and he made a point about how a dedicated anti-fate faction needs to be a bit unsavoury otherwise the Sidereals end up as <i>their</i> antagonists rather than the other way around.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, to me, suggests a much deeper underlying problem with Sidereals if the only way they can come across as sympathetic is if their adversaries are visibly-flawed <i>as people</i>. Honestly I\u2019d like to see some better reasons to care about Destiny in Exalted than \u201cnecessary for some incredibly-mumbly reason about Creation melting without it\u201d and \u201cbecause FUCK YOU, that\u2019s why!\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T13:33:37-07:00","id":1248192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1248180#post1248180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This, to me, suggests a much deeper underlying problem with Sidereals if the only way they can come across as sympathetic is if their adversaries are visibly-flawed <i>as people</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, everybody's flawed as people. That's people for ya.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T13:52:22-07:00","id":1248204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1248163#post1248163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I will have to just disagree, they come from a place of &quot;we need rival exalts&quot; which I think is a terrible premise. There could have been a bunch of ways to introduce them but I can't say I enjoyed the way the core introduced them.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair part of the present problem is we don't know much about the Gets. We knew Rakan found them, not made, and that they're his newest and biggest tool for war on Yu Shan. Hell even the whole pattern spider mini loom that seems to be a thing for all the Getimian we honestly don't if that's a thing the exaltation does ,a la infernal's unbound coadjutor; a qualification, like an artificial way to make someone count as being a descendant of a dragonblood; or if day one of being a Getimian exalt involves horribly invasive surgery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T14:00:00-07:00","id":1248207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1248180#post1248180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This, to me, suggests a much deeper underlying problem with Sidereals if the only way they can come across as sympathetic is if their adversaries are visibly-flawed <i>as people</i>. Honestly I\u2019d like to see some better reasons to care about Destiny in Exalted than \u201cnecessary for some incredibly-mumbly reason about Creation melting without it\u201d and \u201cbecause FUCK YOU, that\u2019s why!\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>Thulio's backstory isn't strictly necessary. I'm just saying the notion of him being John's gary stu self insert is really dubious to me based on a conversation where he said he wasn't going to throw the Sidereals under the bus to make the new guys look cool.<br /> <br /> The thing about the anti-fate faction needing to be a bit unsavoury is that your anti-fate guys are just popping up and minding their own business until they get lynched by Sidereals, then the Sidereals are the fucking bad guys in this story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 08-20-2018, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T14:21:25-07:00","id":1248214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1248192#post1248192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude, everybody's flawed as people. That's people for ya.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe his point is<br /> <br /> 'If the only reason this guy is the villain is because as a person he's a dick', then that's not a compelling villain; if the only reason his plan is unpalatable is because of him personally being a shithead, then he's not doing anyone any favors. I'm not saying Rakan Thulio IS this, but I'm saying that I think that's what Tesaurasaurus is saying and that I would agree if that's what he's saying.<br /> <br /> and to clarify, I consider that different from 'this guy wants to make the world a better place but he's going to kill a million people to do it'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T15:43:55-07:00","id":1248233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flare</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1248214#post1248214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe his point is<br /> <br /> 'If the only reason this guy is the villain is because as a person he's a dick', then that's not a compelling villain; if the only reason his plan is unpalatable is because of him personally being a shithead, then he's not doing anyone any favors. I'm not saying Rakan Thulio IS this, but I'm saying that I think that's what Tesaurasaurus is saying and that I would agree if that's what he's saying.<br /> <br /> and to clarify, I consider that different from 'this guy wants to make the world a better place but he's going to kill a million people to do it'</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1248207#post1248207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing about the anti-fate faction needing to be a bit unsavoury is that your anti-fate guys are just popping up and minding their own business until they get lynched by Sidereals, then the Sidereals are the fucking bad guys in this story.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is already the state of affairs regarding Solars and Lunars, whose violent opposition to the Realm and Yu-Shan is predicated on the fact that they <i>cannot </i>just pop up and mind their own business because a sizeable percentage of DBs and Sidereals regard their very existence as a crime. It's why I would like to see the Sidereals have more unambiguously-worthwhile responsibilities outside of leading death-squads and getting into bureaucratic pissing-matches with deities, because otherwise Sidereals will be the fucking bad guys of the Getimian story by virtue of being fucking bad guys, period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T16:26:30-07:00","id":1248243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1248120#post1248120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Getimians have an awesome hook that could make them a fan favourite (it really depends on if Exigents takes or if we get a repeat of Devil Tigers where most of the energy gets spent on telling people they're doing it wrong). It's been heavily hinted at over the years but never stated outright.</div> </div> </div> </div>All someone needs to do is ask me at a convention. I can't <i>not</i> tell the truth at a convention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T17:42:04-07:00","id":1248254,"title":"","content":"Wow, I did not expect that much conversation from my post. <br /> <br /> It's funny because I actually have a world of mine of my own with heavy Exalted influence (no actual equivalents to Exalted though) that has its own faction of anti-fate dudes, started by a guy whose husband fell deathly ill and then was stymied at every turn due to Heaven's decree that his husband <i>must</i> die. He did everything he could but when his husband died he eventually told Heaven to fuck itself and dedicated his time training other people who had been screwed over by fate to destroying it. Which is basically Thulio's backstory with some tweaks (though Getimians seem to be people who <i>never existed</i> as opposed to getting fucked over by fate), honestly, but if I might be narcissistic I like it more than Exalted's take on it for the reasons I mentioned earlier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T17:45:17-07:00","id":1248256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1248243#post1248243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All someone needs to do is ask me at a convention. I can't <i>not</i> tell the truth at a convention.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But you can lie in a forum post...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T19:35:08-07:00","id":1248275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1248063#post1248063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not so much a question, but I notice that - for the moment - we have a whole <i>Splat: The Upcoming</i> focused on the exploits of one particular guy. That's a pretty distinct difference, in that other splats orbit around their Celestine++ patrons.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Getimian book will not focus on the exploits of Rakan Thulio. It'll focus on the Getimians. They're the protagonists of their stories, not him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-20T20:17:03-07:00","id":1248284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1248233#post1248233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, this is correct.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is already the state of affairs regarding Solars and Lunars, whose violent opposition to the Realm and Yu-Shan is predicated on the fact that they <i>cannot </i>just pop up and mind their own business because a sizeable percentage of DBs and Sidereals regard their very existence as a crime. It's why I would like to see the Sidereals have more unambiguously-worthwhile responsibilities outside of leading death-squads and getting into bureaucratic pissing-matches with deities, because otherwise Sidereals will be the fucking bad guys of the Getimian story by virtue of being fucking bad guys, period.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to say, this viewpoint really resonated with me:<br /> <br /> Sidereals are...<br /> <br /> Solars: Enigmatic Martial Arts Sifu at best, back stabbing traitor baseline (once they hear about Ursupation)<br /> <br /> Lunars: Literal splat antagonists<br /> <br /> Getimians: Literal splat antagonists<br /> <br /> Dragonblooded: Ignorance or Faceless puppeteer overlords in the shadows, take your pick.<br /> <br /> *Remembers that scene from Mitchell and Webb where 2 Nazi SS officers finally realise that they are, for all their smart trappings, the bad guys.*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 08-21-2018, 04:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T01:20:52-07:00","id":1248349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1248132#post1248132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, but it's agonising that a topic about one of the coolest things I was told about for Ex3 ends up as a discussion of Rakan Thulio's sex life.</div> </div> </div> </div>I definitely sympathise with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T01:57:32-07:00","id":1248358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1248233#post1248233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, this is correct.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is already the state of affairs regarding Solars and Lunars, whose violent opposition to the Realm and Yu-Shan is predicated on the fact that they <i>cannot </i>just pop up and mind their own business because a sizeable percentage of DBs and Sidereals regard their very existence as a crime. It's why I would like to see the Sidereals have more unambiguously-worthwhile responsibilities outside of leading death-squads and getting into bureaucratic pissing-matches with deities, because otherwise Sidereals will be the fucking bad guys of the Getimian story by virtue of being fucking bad guys, period.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe one of their duties this edition is handling it when exigence has been stolen considering the potential nightmare an exigent can create not counting the standard policing of gods and spirit courts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T11:24:24-07:00","id":1248472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1248275#post1248275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Getimian book will not focus on the exploits of Rakan Thulio. It'll focus on the Getimians. They're the protagonists of their stories, not him.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me happy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">https://swordofcreation.net/</a> : A secondary forum focusing on archiving homebrew, both mechanical and fluff, and receiving critique on it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/108-flare","name":"Flare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar108_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T19:22:07-07:00","id":1248599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1248132#post1248132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, but it's agonising that a topic about one of the coolest things I was told about for Ex3 ends up as a discussion of Rakan Thulio's sex life.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that, right now, pretty much all the official info we have about Getimians consists of details about Rakan Thulio\u2019s sex life, I can understand why conversations trend that way.<br /> <br /> As for the coolest thing, I\u2019m hoping it has something to do with alternate dimensions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-22T03:02:10-07:00","id":1248664,"title":"","content":"For the sake of internet threads, we need more info on Getimians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-22T11:30:52-07:00","id":1248755,"title":"","content":"I'm rather put in the mind of the antagonist of the Sanderson Cosmere novel Elantris when I hear of Rakan Thulio's backstory. The same rage against the heavens, with a perhaps-more-sympathetic origin but perhaps much worse implementation of the war.<br /> <br /> As for the Getimians as a splat, I feel almost as if they're threads snipped out of the Loom of Fate. I am reminded vividly of Fate in Piers Anthony's With A Tangled Skein when they're first trying to learn their powers. The pattern spider that maintains the thread outside of the Loom--presumably jettisoned along with the thread--would be a Fate analog of the demon that merged with an Infernal's soul in (at least 2E) Infernals. If true, the Getimians would be even more an analogous to the Infernal role to the Sidereals. That is,<br /> <br /> Solar : Infernal :: Sidereal : Getimian<br /> <br /> but even more... ambiguous.<br /> <br /> Also, it may be that the Getimians do not want to break the Loom so much as repair it... that is, to reintegrate themselves into the Loom so that the Getimian/thread will exist without the intervention of the pattern spiders. Specifically, if Getimians are 'fates that should not be', their entire arc could (should?) be to change that to 'fate that should be / is'. And naturally, if the threads in the Loom were cut for good reason, they could wreak catastrophic damage to Creation to do this.<br /> <br /> ... really stretching here, but wouldn't it be awesome if there was a Getimian somewhere who, if reintegrated into the Loom, <i>reversed</i> the Usurpation or caused it not to happen? So, you know, all those threads (heh, NPI) about the Sidereal decisions, and there was something who could <i>actually show/know</i> not what happened, but what <i>might have happened</i>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-22T19:24:47-07:00","id":1248808,"title":"","content":"I'm wondering if they might have been originally intended to play a role somewhat similar to Oversight in 2E Sidereals, operating as an outside check on the Bureau of Destiny, independent from Fate but intimately familiar with its workings; the &quot;Who Watches the Watchers?&quot; to the Fivefold Fellowship. Though that would, of course, raise questions as to why they were... set aside? cast out? ...before Thulio rediscovered them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-23T00:24:27-07:00","id":1248822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ascension</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1248808#post1248808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering if they might have been originally intended to play a role somewhat similar to Oversight in 2E Sidereals, operating as an outside check on the Bureau of Destiny, independent from Fate but intimately familiar with its workings; the &amp;quot;Who Watches the Watchers?&amp;quot; to the Fivefold Fellowship. Though that would, of course, raise questions as to why they were... set aside? cast out? ...before Thulio rediscovered them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oversite was a garbage idea. One that was done to downgrade the sidereals from the secret masters of the world to the sort of but not really secret masters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-23T01:31:07-07:00","id":1248825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ascension</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1248808#post1248808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wondering if they might have been originally intended to play a role somewhat similar to Oversight in 2E Sidereals, operating as an outside check on the Bureau of Destiny, independent from Fate but intimately familiar with its workings; the &quot;Who Watches the Watchers?&quot; to the Fivefold Fellowship. Though that would, of course, raise questions as to why they were... set aside? cast out? ...before Thulio rediscovered them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Word of dev has said the Getimians aren't cousins to the Sidereals; the only thing Vance has revealed of their creators - aside from his use of the plural - is that even the Maidens fear them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-26T10:02:44-07:00","id":1248971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1248825#post1248825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Word of dev has said the Getimians aren't cousins to the Sidereals; the only thing Vance has revealed of their creators - aside from his use of the plural - is that even the Maidens fear them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's right. I completely forgot about that.<br /> <br /> That's very odd in conjunction with them having internal Pattern Spiders, however. Unless their creators are replacing Autochthon as the original creators of the Pattern Spiders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21733-ascension","name":"Ascension","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21733_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T00:27:14-07:00","id":1249072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ascension</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1246864-getimians-what-am-i-supposed-to-do-with-them?p=1248971#post1248971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, that's right. I completely forgot about that.<br /> <br /> That's very odd in conjunction with them having internal Pattern Spiders, however. Unless their creators are replacing Autochthon as the original creators of the Pattern Spiders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there had to be some reason there weren't Getimians all along after their Exaltations were created, and thus something that had to be done to get them (back?) into circulation. Perhaps the internal Pattern Spiders, instead of an intrinsic feature, are Rakan Thulio's hack to get around whatever disabled them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}